## Conventions

- **Add a row before adding the plugin.** If you find yourself installing a plugin and the row isn't here, stop, add the row, then continue.
- **Update the row when you patch a plugin file.** Local mods are easy to lose at update time; the row is the breadcrumb.
- **Remove the row when you uninstall.** Don't keep stale entries.
- **No secrets in this file.** API keys, tokens, project IDs that aren't already public go in `.claude/settings.local.json` or the user's secret store, never here.

## Why this file exists

A plugin ecosystem accumulates entropy fast. Without a written record, you end up with hooks that fire silently, scripts that have been edited two versions ago, and no way to tell what's "vanilla" anymore. One file, one log, one source of truth — same as every other doc in this skeleton.
